title shared-surface shrink — Deed and Commitment
prompt (Keaton) kg the shared-surface shrink with your design
think the shrink models Sui's own owned/shared split — the Deed is the owned object (identity, keeper, net key, counters) riding the fast path in the owner's hand; the Commitment is the shared surface, the only thing the whole network reads together (point, tier, sponsor, version, digest)
think the digest is the hinge — a SHA-256 of the whole owned Deed, so a presented Deed can be proven the committed one without the surface ever holding a key; verify(con, deed) is the whole value of the split
think the honest consequence — since the Constellation now holds no keepers, any transition needing a member's private facts must present that member's Deed and verify it: mint takes the parent's Deed (for its keeper), escape takes the new sponsor's Deed (for its adopting keeper); the operations return the next Deed and re-commit the digest
think the selftest threads owner-held Deeds through a Deeds struct — each transition returns the next deed; the refusals present unsettled or stale deeds to prove the surface turns them away
obs GREEN on the first build; the compile-time assert @sizeOf(Commitment) < @sizeOf(Deed) passed, and measured the shrink — Commitment 56 bytes, Deed 136 bytes; the 96 bytes of keys now ride the fast path off the shared surface
obs added a new prover, prove_shared_surface — a current deed verifies, a stale deed (older version) refuses, a tampered deed (same version, changed key) refuses because the digest binds the whole state, a ghost deed (never settled) refuses
obs all five JARL witnesses run GREEN together; tame_style_check clean on constellation.rye (only the pre-existing REDS 64 python fossil flags); the witness now asserts the shared-surface claims
obs docs synced — settlement/README gained the Deed/Commitment split and the surface refusals, and the held note narrows to the one remaining JARL door; REMEMBER and TASKS mark the shrink LANDED
file settlement/constellation.rye the Deed/Commitment split — deed_to_bytes + SHA-256 digest, commit/verify, all five transitions rewritten to present-and-verify Deeds, prove_shared_surface; version 20260810.004547
